//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
//
// Prototype table for all __metal_* stdlib entry points seen in Apple's
// metal_stdlib headers (kagurasumusun/metal-info -> 686 unique symbols).
//
// Design rationale
// ================
//
// Apple's proprietary Metal clang treats every ``__metal_*`` name as a
// compiler-recognised intrinsic whose signature is *inferred from the call
// site*.  The same ``__metal_fabs`` for example appears at call sites with
// one, two, or three arguments, and with argument types ranging from
// ``float`` to ``half8`` to a Metal-specific overloaded scalar.  A single
// C prototype cannot satisfy all of them.
//
// Our own clang cannot yet re-implement Apple's implicit intrinsic
// declaration mechanism, but the Apple stdlib STILL parses and INSTANTIATES
// through us at every call site.  We therefore inject a permissive
// declaration that
//   (a) accepts any number and type of arguments (C++ variadic template),
//   (b) is implicitly convertible to any expected return type via the
//       ``__clang_metal_any_t`` proxy defined by InitPreprocessor.cpp, and
//   (c) still lets CGMetalBuiltins.cpp / CGExpr.cpp dispatch on the name
//       (``getDirectCallee()->getName()``) because template specialisation
//       preserves the identifier.
//
// The texture helpers listed below are the sole exception: they are
// declared inline (typed) by InitPreprocessor.cpp so that
// ``CGExpr.cpp::getMetalTextureHelperLoweringName`` can lower them to
// dedicated ``air.texture.*`` intrinsics without going through the generic
// ``EmitMetalBuiltinExpr`` path.  We therefore omit them here to avoid
// duplicate declarations.
//
// METAL_STDLIB_BUILTIN_PROTO(Name, PrototypeString)
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

#ifndef METAL_STDLIB_BUILTIN_PROTO
#define METAL_STDLIB_BUILTIN_PROTO(Name, PrototypeString)
#endif

METAL_STDLIB_BUILTIN_PROTO(__metal_abort_intersection_query, "template<class... __M_A> inline ::__clang_metal_any_t __metal_abort_intersection_query(__M_A&&...) noexcept;")
